&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Day 1: Coyhaique to Puerto Rio Tranquillo</title><link>https://jonathan-baruch.github.io/out-of-sandbox/posts/day1/</link><pubDate>Tue, 10 Mar 2026 23:43:21 -0300</pubDate><guid>https://jonathan-baruch.github.io/out-of-sandbox/posts/day1/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;After yesterday&amp;rsquo;s travels, I decided to sleep in some more today and enjoy a bit of this quiant Hostel made up of old typewriters, a fireplace, and sliding doors counter-weighted by knitted hens. I hit the road by 8AM to get a headstart on the day since I would have the long drive ahead of me. I grabbed gas at the local Copec Station and began my way down South for Puerto Rio Tranquillo, but had no idea what magic the day had in store for me.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>